==Russian==
{{wp|ru:}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|годъ||ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*gʰedʰ-}}
From {{inh|ru|orv|годъ||time, period, year, age}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*godъ||suitable time}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-bsl-pro|*gadás}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*gʰodʰo-}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*gʰedʰ-||to unite, be associated, be suitable}}.

Cognates include
{{cog|uk|годі||enough}},
{{cog|bg|годе||[[ever]]}} (as in {{l|bg|кой-годе}} = whoever),
{{cog|cs|hod}},
{{cog|pl|gody||yearly feast}},
{{cog|hsb|hody||Christmas}},
{{cog|dsb|gódy||Christmas}},
{{cog|lv|gadigs}}.

Germanic cognates include
{{cog|de|Gatte||husband}}, {{m|de|gätlich||convenient}},
{{cog|nl|gegade}}, {{m|nl|gade}}, {{m|nl|gading}},
{{cog|nl|gader}}, {{m|nl|goed}},
{{cog|de|gut}}, as well as {{cog|en|gather}}, {{m|en|together}} and {{m|en|good}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-год.ogg}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush-год.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}
* {{homophones|ru|гот}}
* {{rhymes|ru|ot|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|e|or|c||(1)|or|c||(1)(2)|лет|par=+|loc=в +|adj=годи́чный|dim=го́дик,годо́к}}

# [[year]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[из го́да в год]]|year in and year out, from year to year}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[в]] [[этот|э́том]] '''году́'''|this year}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[года́ми]]|for years; for years on end}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[девяностый|девяно́стые]] '''го́ды'''|the '90s}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[уче́бный]] '''год'''|school year; academic year}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[новый|Но́вый]] '''год'''|New Year’s Day}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Ему́]] [[два́дцать оди́н]] '''год'''.|He is 21 years old.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Ему́]] [[два́дцать три]] '''го́да'''.|He is 23 years old.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Ему́]] [[два́дцать пять]] [[лето|лет]].|He is 25 years old.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[ты́сяча]] [[девятьсо́т]] [[девяно́сто]] [[второ́й]] '''год'''|(year) 1992 {{q|in words}}}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[два|две]] [[тысяча|ты́сячи]] [[оди́ннадцатый]] '''год'''|(year) 2011 {{q|in words}}}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[с]] [[каждый|ка́ждым]] '''го́дом'''|from year to year, year by year, year after year}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[по]] [[сравнение|сравне́нию]] [[с]] [[тот же|те́м же]] [[период|пери́одом]] [[прошлый|про́шлого]] '''го́да'''|as compared to the corresponding period last year, from the same time last year}}

====Usage notes====
* When the genitive plural is used after a cardinal number, the word {{m|ru|лет|pos=genitive plural of {{m|ru|ле́то||summer}}}} is used instead of {{m|ru|годо́в}}. This applies to numbers whose names do not end in {{m|ru|оди́н||one}}, {{m|ru|два||two}}, {{m|ru|три||three}}, or {{m|ru|четы́ре||four}} when in the nominative, genitive, or accusative case (so this includes numbers like 114 whose name in Russian does not end in ''четы́ре''), as well as to numbers ending in {{m|ru|два}}, {{m|ru|три}}, or {{m|ru|четы́ре}} in genitive case.
* To put this in another way, when a number should be followed by a nominative or genitive singular, the appropriate form of {{m|ru|год}} is used. When a number should be followed by a genitive plural, the form {{m|ru|лет}} is used. When the number is in the dative, instrumental, or prepositional case, the appropriate form of {{m|ru|год}} must be used. Examples: {{m|ru||оди́н год|pos=nominative singular}}, {{m|ru||два го́да|pos=genitive singular}}, {{m|ru||три го́да|pos=genitive singular}}, {{m|ru||пять лет|pos=genitive plural}}; but {{m|ru||бо́льше трёх лет|pos=genitive plural}}, {{m|ru||бо́льше пяти́ лет|pos=genitive plural}}; and {{m|ru||пяти́ года́м|pos=dative plural}}, {{m|ru||пятью́ года́ми|pos=instrumental plural}}, {{m|ru||o пяти́ года́х|pos=prepositional plural}}.
* When used with an ordinal number, the above rules do not apply, and one simply uses the non-suppletive form of {{m|ru||год}}. For example, {{m|ru||в нача́ле девяно́стых годо́в|at the beginning of the '90s}}.

